---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { app, includedTools, plans, site } from "../data/site";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Organization",
      name: site.name,
      url: site.url,
      logo: `${site.url}/brand/wordmark.png`,
      description: site.description,
      telephone: site.phoneTel,
      sameAs: [site.x, site.instagram],
    },
    {
      "@type": "WebSite",
      name: site.name,
      url: site.url,
    },
    {
      "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
      name: "AgentOS",
      applicationCategory: "BusinessApplication",
      operatingSystem: "Web",
      offers: plans.map((plan) => ({
        "@type": "Offer",
        name: plan.name,
        price: String(plan.price),
        priceCurrency: "USD",
      })),
    },
  ],
};
---

<Base title={site.title} path="/">
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="head" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />

  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="address">
      <span class="num">1428</span>
      <span class="street">Cedar Street</span>
    </p>
    <div class="story">
      <p>
        Thursday evening. Maya Chen is buying with you. $640k to $720k, two
        bedrooms, elevator, walkable. Match 91. The call is done. You confirm
        6:40.
      </p>
      <h1 class="pitch">
        AgentOS is the workspace for the rest of the practice: CRM, calling,
        matching, marketing, and client portals.
      </h1>
      <a class="btn" href={app.signup}>Get started</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter wrap" id="who">
    <h2>Professionals run the paid workspace.</h2>
    <p>
      Agents, brokers, and teams use AgentOS for clients, leads, listings,
      marketing, follow-up, and transactions. This account is not for someone
      buying or selling their own property. Paid plans, except authorized owner
      or pre-launch access.
    </p>
    <a class="btn" href={app.signupPro}>Get started as a professional</a>
    <p class="else">
      Buying with an agent? <a class="text-go" href={app.signupBuyer}>Free buyer account</a>
    </p>
    <p class="else">
      Selling with an agent? <a class="text-go" href={app.signupSeller}>Free seller account</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter wrap" id="product">
    <h2>A lead does not sit in an inbox.</h2>
    <p class="mute">
      The assistant can call, text, and qualify. Every action writes back to the
      CRM. You take the appointment.
    </p>
    <div class="flow">
      <p>The lead is captured.</p>
      <p>It is qualified.</p>
      <p>Follow-up is prepared.</p>
      <p>A showing or appointment is requested.</p>
      <p>You take the handoff.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="mute">
      Calling, email, and SMS depend on consent, applicable law, plan allowances,
      and the connected provider. Simulated outcomes stay separate from production
      records.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter wrap" id="create">
    <h2>Keep the file moving, then turn the listing into a campaign.</h2>
    <p>
      Pipelines, activity, tasks, listings, showing requests, the Seller Portal,
      and buyer matching stay in one place. From confirmed listing details you
      can prepare visuals, captions, campaign plans, and property pages.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a client needs another market, you pass a protected note through the
      network. Jordan in Austin needs a Denver listing agent. Priya takes the
      referral. The conversation stays inside AgentOS.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter wrap">
    <h2>Nothing is public until you publish it.</h2>
    <p>
      The marketplace only shows listings you mark public, or records from
      permitted providers. Private CRM data, unpublished properties, messages,
      and seller files stay in the workspace. Seller submissions need
      professional review. AgentOS is not an MLS, and MLS, IDX, CPAR, and
      Trestle connectivity are not in this launch.
    </p>
    <a class="text-go" href={app.marketplace}>Open the public marketplace</a>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter wrap" id="pricing">
    <h2>Same tools. Different capacity.</h2>
    <p class="mute">
      Plans differ by credits, automation volume, seats, and limits. Paid access
      turns on after payment is confirmed on the server.
    </p>
    <div class="rates">
      {plans.map((plan) => (
        <a class="rate" href={app.signupPro}>
          <b>{plan.name}</b>
          <strong>${plan.price.toLocaleString("en-US")} a month</strong>
          <span>{plan.blurb}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p>
      Every paid plan can include {includedTools.slice(0, -1).join(", ")}, and{" "}
      {includedTools[includedTools.length - 1].toLowerCase()}.
    </p>
    <a class="text-go" href="/pricing">Full plan notes</a>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter wrap" id="contact">
    <h2>Call or write.</h2>
    <p class="phone"><a href={`tel:${site.phoneTel}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a></p>
    <p>
      <a class="text-go" href={site.whatsapp} rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp</a> or
      the <a class="text-go" href="/support">support form</a>. Use
      <a class="text-go" href={app.abuse}>Report abuse</a> for suspicious
      marketplace content or harassment. Never send passwords, API keys, or card
      numbers.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
